  "visibleTextNormalized": "HomeOur community Our Community Fort Street has a strong and supportive community of both past and present students and families. Fort Street Alumni Fort Street Alumni Community members of work with the school to archive and display important records, memorabilia and documents in our museum from all three schools throughout history. east The Parents and Citizens Association (P&C) The P&C is highly active and contributes substantially to the life of Fort Street High School. It provides a forum which enables parents to get involved in the organisation and direction of the school. east The Fort Street Foundation The Fort Street Foundation a registered charity and supports the school financially for initiatives including the development of buildings and facilities. east The Fortians Union The Fortian Union began in 1894 and promotes social fellowship, reunions, assists the school and preserves its traditions. east Have a question for our principal or teachers? Our friendly office team can help you get in touch. Contact us Learning Find out about our approach to learning and supporting students to progress. east Travel to school Learn about local transport options and how to get here safely. east Section navigation About us Contact us Learning and support Our community Alumni Foundation Tertiary Bursaries Parents and Citizens Association The Fort Street Foundation The Fortians Union School life",
